latest_quarter.body:
- **Q1 FY27 (this):** Global business INR 17.55 lakh cr (+16.57%); global deposits INR 9.58 lakh cr (+14.90%);
  global gross advances INR 7.98 lakh cr (+18.64%); RAM INR 3.93 lakh cr (+19.75%, 58.30% of advances);
  CASA INR 3.02 lakh cr, **CASA ratio 36.68%** (−~3% YoY); NII INR 6,833 cr (+12.61%); non-interest income
  INR 2,579 cr (+19.07%); operating profit INR 5,051 cr (+25.99%); **net profit INR 3,068 cr (+36.23%)**;
  **NIM 2.52% (vs 2.55%)**; **GNPA 1.81% / NNPA 0.51%**; **PCR 93.83%**; **slippage 0.24%**; **credit cost 0.15%**;
  **CRAR 18.69%**; ROA ~1%; CIR ~46%; SMA ≥INR 5 cr INR 4,090 cr (0.52% of standard book); international business
  ~INR 2.56 lakh cr (first time >2.5 lakh cr); gold loan book ~INR 57,000 cr (+52% YoY, yield ~9.10%, NPA <INR 100 cr);
  digital sanctions 22% of domestic credit; ECLGS INR 6,000 cr sanctioned / INR 4,600 cr disbursed;
  FCNR(B) >USD 200 mn of a USD 1.2 bn / 30-Sep-2026 target. No AS-15 reversal taken. Guidance unchanged:
  advances 15–16%, deposits 13–14%, NIM 2.55–2.60%, ROA ≥1%, CIR 48–49%.
- _Next Q → check: **FCNR(B) actual vs USD 1.2 bn by 30-Sep-2026** (was >USD 200 mn); OFCB/MTN USD 2 bn + ECB
  ~USD 1 bn toward USD 4.2 bn by 31-Dec-2026; whether **NIM recovers into the 2.55–2.60% guide** from 2.52%;
  whether **CIR reverts to 48–49%** from ~46% (i.e. how much of the Q1 beat was cost timing); repeatability of the
  treasury-aided non-interest income; **CASA ratio** stabilisation vs further slide from 36.68%; Q1-peak slippage
  claim ("fresh slippages will go down further in the coming quarters") vs 0.24%; ECLGS run to INR 8,000 cr and what
  MSME slippage does as the scheme winds down; gold-loan book past INR 57,000 cr at ~52% growth; PSL income vs
  INR 277 cr base; credit-card base toward 3 lakh; international book delta given the trade-finance swap-out;
  any movement on PSU-bank merger or BOI Mutual Fund monetisation._
